{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Getting the Client", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Closure", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 11, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 9, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Present advice on solving technical problems in a work context and appropriate for the interlocutor.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le09ob11re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Talking About Experiences: Past Simple and Present Perfect ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "In English, you use the <span class=\"strong\">Past Simple</span> and <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> tenses to talk about experiences. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> tense to talk about a past action or an action that began in the past that is connected to the present in some way.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Past Simple</span> tense to talk about different kinds of past events: short, quickly finished actions, longer situations and repeated events.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> tense to talk about experience. When you use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> tense, you think about the past and present together. There is some connection between what happened in the past and now.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li>Use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> to talk about an action that happened in the past but you do not know when it happened.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">We've settled on a final price. <br/>It's been a pleasure doing business with you. <br/>We have sent one of your staff to South America.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li>Use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span> to talk about something that happened in the past but has a present result.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples: <br/><span class=\"italic\">You've waited until now to tell me this! <br/>We've agreed to provide media coverage for the event.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li>Use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect </span>to talk about things that happened sooner than expected.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">I could be wrong but I think you've already seen the details.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Usually, when you use the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past</span> tense, the time of the finished action is clear from the context or explicitly mentioned in the sentence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">We agreed to provide media coverage for the fashion show next week.</span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Exchanging Opinions ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Conversations are far more interesting when people interact during the conversation. It is important to ask for others' opinions on a subject as well as giving your own. Here are some ways you can exchange opinions. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":1,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Giving Opinions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">When you give opinions, make your opinions less forceful by using neutral statements:</span><br/> <ul><li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">I could</span> ... (+ verb)</li><li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">This/That was</span> ... (+ adjective + noun)</li><li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">I think </span>... (+ clause)</li><li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">I must say I </span>... (+ verb phrase)</li><li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">To be honest</span> ... (+ clause)</li><li>(clause) ... <span class=\\\"italic\\\">if you ask me.</span></li><li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">I could be wrong, but</span> ... (+ clause)</li><li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">I felt that</span>  ... (+ clause)</li></ul>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">I must say</span> we are ready to close the deal.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">I could </span>ask her to get back to you on that matter. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "introductory offer", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the amount that a business suggests as a price for their product or services", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: After your introductory offer, I must say we are ready.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le09ob11aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use making business arrangements.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "seal the deal", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to come to an agreement", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We are ready to seal the deal.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le09ob11aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "training ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the process of teaching people to develop certain skills", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I think we should jot a line about the training needs.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le09ob11aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "personnel ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the people working for a particular company or organization", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Personnel arrangements are something we haven't discussed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le09ob11aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "arrangements ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "practical plans for managing details for things or people", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We haven't discussed the arrangements.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le09ob11aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "in depth", "type": "name"}, {"content": "very detailed, providing much   information", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This is the best method to do in depth market research.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le09ob11aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "leadership ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the position of being leader or in charge of a group", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I am experiencing firsthand the reason for Polygon's leadership in the market.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le09ob11aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to foresee", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be aware of or imagine something before it happens ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I foresee a long-lasting relationship. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le09ob11aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "You are closing a negotiation with an important company.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a dialogue of 6-8 lines.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make sure that in the dialogue you include your opinions.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Close the deal